<h2>Questions from Bear property owners</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Bear isn’t a city. Do you still cover it?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Yes. We cover all of New Castle County, including unincorporated communities such as Bear, Glasgow and Hockessin.</p></div></details><details><summary>My water heater burst. Is that covered?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Sudden water damage from a burst water heater is usually covered, though the water heater itself may not be. We value the resulting damage.</p></div></details><details><summary>Do you handle townhome association claims?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Yes, for both boards and individual owners.</p></div></details></div>
